<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Color" title="Color"
  description="The Color block of FLOAT: colour calibration on the Gaia XP spectra of the field’s stars, the G2V white, which stars are left out, one factor per colour, the fallback balance, settings and limits, with the published sources.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Color</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It sets the colour balance of the image from the stars of the field, whose true colours are known from the Gaia catalogue.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>A neutral sky and stars with their natural colours; Inspect lists every star measured, and whether it was used.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>Usually nothing: the defaults suit most fields; White reference chooses which star colour looks white, and Minimum stars can be lowered for a narrow field with few stars.</dd></div></dl>

  <aside class="note toc">
    <b>On this page</b>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#s1"><span class="secnum">1</span>What goes in, what comes out</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s2"><span class="secnum">2</span>The stars and their spectra</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s3"><span class="secnum">3</span>Measuring the stars</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s4"><span class="secnum">4</span>The white and the factors</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s5"><span class="secnum">5</span>Where the matrix is applied</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s6"><span class="secnum">6</span>The fallback balance</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s7"><span class="secnum">7</span>An approximation of the sensor’s response</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s8"><span class="secnum">8</span>Settings</a></li>
      <li><a href="#s9"><span class="secnum">9</span>Limits, and what was tried</a></li>
